Z||000000||cadaver||06-17-2001||11:53 AM||||This is an email I got sent from a guy telling me how it is.<P>Its for real, PONTIAC owns Lotus but not Isuzu.  Has owned Lotus for more than one Decade.   They used the design "Purchase" to funnel $22,000,000 into Lotus failing budget.  A rather neat way to avoid the tax crunch.  Comes under the heading of creative accounting.  They used the design, Not the Parts. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||06-17-2001||12:42 PM||||GM, not Pontiac <I>owned</I> Lotus (past tense). <BR>Lotus designed the ZR1 engine (Mercury Marine built it), and assisted in suspension designs for Pontiac and Isuzu, who was in a "partnership" of sorts, with GM. (GM owned like 35% of Isuzu at the time). GM produced the suspension parts to Lotus' design. <P>Lotus is again struggling, and the M250 project (Esprit replacement) seems to be on hold. I would expect to see Lotus for sale again within 2 years. <P>Hope that helps.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||06-17-2001||11:36 PM||||The M250 is freaking gorgeous. Looks like an Elise on steroids. Too bad that it's "on hold".<BR>At one time I thought that <I>it</I> might become a new Fiero (or Saturn). More the Fiero's size than the Elise is. <BR>Until I read that it was going to sell for around $60K US.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
